id well shootin and I mean I'm four  years removed from high school coaching  I don't know that's not gonna happen he  goes we'll do it and so I I did it I  mean I reached out and I got an  interview and interview with coach Walsh  and and all the coaches out there in San  Francisco grew up there of course and  then they said you know bill was very  honest with me said you know I have a  couple guys in mind and and you know you  did a good job but if this other fellow  wants the job I think I'm gonna go that  way and so I said great thanks for the  opportunity which was kind of what I  thought it was gonna be  I came back to BYU and I'm out jogging  one day I was there two weeks and and  the secretary goes Mitch Walsh phoned I  told him you were out jogging what what  did you do well you said you'd phoned  back okay good wherever I am grab me get  me and so then bill Foley said listen  would you like to take we'd like to hire  you and I said well I got talked to so  yeah go on instead of screaming and  yelling on the phone I said I gotta talk  this over with Cathy and just make sure  he goes okay I'll talk to you tonight at  home so I went home and said hey we got  a chance and sure enough I got the job  so coming back to this city I grew up in  and was very special coaching for Bill  Walsh and then coaching Joe Montana  right yes that's the gig yeah that's the  gig I I want to  tell your wrist so that until I got  there Joe wasn't very good that's right  he's coachable don't forget that right  no I did another another quick story  that I I was wondering how I'm what I'm  gonna how can I help Joe is what I'm  thinking he this guy's great he's won  MVP Super Bowls and all this kind of  stuff and and bill came up to me one day  I'd been there about two weeks  it was the offseason of course and he  goes this and Joe's coming over while  you guys grab a cup of coffee and you  know talking and get to know each other  so I said okay it's gonna be good I'm  nervous I kind 